{{Short description|Football tournament group stage}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=May 2018}}
'''Group 4 of the [[1966 FIFA World Cup]]''' consisted of [[Chile national football team|Chile]], [[Soviet Union national football team|Soviet Union]], [[Italy national football team|Italy]], and [[North Korea national football team|North Korea]]. Play began on 12 July 1966 and concluded on 20 July 1966. Soviet Union won the group and North Korea finished as runners-up on their World Cup debut, and both advanced to the quarter-finals. Italy and Chile failed to advance.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Stokkermans |first1=Karel |last2=Jarreta |first2=Sergio Henrique |url=https://www.rsssf.org/tables/66f.html |title=World Cup 1966 (England, July 11–30) |website=RSSSF.com |publisher=[[Rec.Sport.Soccer Statistics Foundation]] |date=22 October 1999 |access-date=26 May 2018}}</ref>

